  "articleBody": "After a Texas windstorm, it's natural to scan your roof for damage. But how do you tell if what you're seeing is fresh wind damage or just regular wear and tear that's accumulated over time? This distinction is crucial, especially when considering repairs or an insurance claim. Wind damage can often be subtle, like lifted shingle tabs or missing granules, which might look like aging at first glance. However, attributing all roof wear to a single storm is a common mistake that can complicate things. You need to understand the tell-tale signs to properly assess your roof's condition and take appropriate action.\n\nWind damage tends to show up in specific patterns. Look for creased or torn shingles, especially those along ridges, hips, and eaves. Missing shingles are an obvious sign, but sometimes the damage is more hidden, like displaced flashing around chimneys or vents. Granule loss, particularly when it exposes the asphalt mat underneath, is another indicator. Normal wear, on the other hand, usually appears as widespread, even deterioration across the roof surface, often accompanied by general fading or moss growth. A professional inspection can definitively distinguish between these, identifying potential issues before they become costly repairs. Discounted Roofing Co. provides clear answers and practical recommendations.\n\n### When Professional Guidance Helps\nWhile you can do a preliminary check, professional guidance becomes invaluable when distinguishing between wind damage and normal wear. A qualified professional is especially important when the cause of damage is disputed, or when the damage is concealed or structural. They have the expertise to spot subtle signs that homeowners might miss and can accurately assess the roof's age and prior condition. Furthermore, if you suspect multiple building components beyond just the roof have been affected, or if the evaluation needs to support an insurance claim, an expert assessment is critical. Discounted Roofing Co. offers professional inspections and storm-damage assessments, ensuring you get dependable workmanship and straightforward communication.\n\nIf you're unsure about the state of your roof after high winds in the Dallas-Fort Worth area, don't hesitate to contact Discounted Roofing Co. Our experienced team can provide a clear and honest evaluation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}